    ('A24',
     'Very cool place and great hosts! Area is gorgeous…hard to leave! Thank you!',
     'Alison · Lavonia, GA', 'November 2025'),
    ('A25',
     'Speechless! Cannot put into words how gorgeous everything was! Felt very welcomed. We came from Florida to bring our grandkids on a little vacation. I was so surprised when after communicating to Mike and Livvy our hopes for the weekend, they sent a FULL ITINERARY! Starting with leave time from Atlanta to apple picking and pumpkin picking, gold mine, items to bring for grandkids…. The home made pizza dinner the grandkids made in the tree tops was delicious, and fun! I would recommend this to everyone from a couples romantic get a way to family of 4. It was indescribable! None of us wanted to leave! Next time we will stay longer! Thank you for your hospitality and kindness!',
     'Mary · Naples, FL', 'October 2025'),
    ('A26',
     'Beautiful, magical, wonderful place to camp with a few extra amenities that make it more like glamping! This place is very special, and if you are looking for a place to unwind and unplug, and hike/play in the creek, this is it. Staying in this treehouse is a unique experience and all the extra touches the hosts add are top notch. We had such an amazing time and got some amazing family time in.\n\nPro tips: ask for the homemade pizza dough, it’s delicious. Bring some speciality toppings to take it another level. Splurge on the morning breakfast option with mimosas, it is worth every penny. Whatever food you bring to cook, be prepared to cook it over an open fire at the fire pit. Bring flash lights! The bed and the extra mattress are very comfortable, sleeps 3 fairly comfortably (we had 4). Bathroom is very clean and lovely to have while camping, expect an unconventional toilet and shower combo. Overall, highly recommend this place if you are looking for a family adventure!!',
     'Alaina · Gainesville, GA', 'October 2025'),
    ('A27',
     'Had a great time celebrating a special occasion at the treehouse. Livy and Mike were amazing hosts. The pastries and pizza dough were amazing and definitely recommend one of the additional packages if you want to splurge.\n\nThey also had some great local recommendations and were very responsive.\n\nThe treehouse itself was incredible, I think it’s hard to convey over a picture. We had a good time watching a movie outside and enjoying the nature from the treehouse.\n\nAs for the location, it’s a convenient 10-15 minutes from downtown Dahlonega and close to a trail and a winery.\n\nCouldn’t have asked for more with our weekend and would highly recommend to anyone considering a stay!',
     'Kristian · Athens, GA', 'September 2025'),
    ('A28',
     'What can I say about this property…words cannot do it justice - you need to experience it! The location itself is spectacular, with paths winding through the forest, birdsong in the mornings and the sound of the water below is so relaxing!\n\nI won’t spoil the surprises that the hosts offer you, but believe me you will be very pleased with their thoughtfulness. They truly go above and beyond to make you feel welcome and comfortable, communicate effectively and will even draft you an itinerary of suggestions for the surrounding area. They’ve thought of everything!\n\nThank you both for having us, we will be back! :)',
     'Megan · Mobile, AL', 'September 2025'),
